```java
public final class Inputs {
    private static final Pattern DECIMAL = Pattern.compile("^-?\\d{1,30}(\\.\\d{1,6})?$");
    public static String requireText(String value, String field) { ... 400 }
    public static BigDecimal requireDecimal(String value, String field) { ... }
    public static Instant requireInstant(String value, String field) { Instant.parse or OffsetDateTime parse }
}
```

For instant parsing: accept ISO-8601 with offset. Use `OffsetDateTime.parse` fallback `Instant.parse`? Simplest: `Instant.parse` accepts only 'Z'. Better: use `DateTimeFormatter.ISO_OFFSET_DATE_TIME` → OffsetDateTime → toInstant. That accepts "2026-09-21T10:00:00Z" and "+08:00" offsets. Good.

