@Transactional
public Measurement submit(SubmitMeasurementRequest req) {
    validate all fields, lower<=upper
    Certificate cert = certRepo.findMatching(instrumentId, measuredAt).orElseThrow(422);
    BigDecimal computed = cert.a().multiply(reading).add(cert.b());
    boolean passed = computed.compareTo(lower) >= 0 && computed.compareTo(upper) <= 0;
    Measurement m = new Measurement(0, key, ..., computed, passed, PENDING, now);
    try { long id = repo.insert(m); } catch (DuplicateKeyException e) { throw conflict("DUPLICATE_MEASUREMENT_KEY"); }
    return repo.findByKey(key).orElseThrow();
}
```

Note computed value scale: a (scale ≤6) × reading (scale ≤6) → scale ≤12; + b (scale ≤6) → scale ≤12. Fits DECIMAL(38,12). But BigDecimal from DB: coeff_a DECIMAL(38,6) returns scale 6. multiply gives scale 12. add gives scale max(12,6)=12. Fine.

